I
摘要
当前我国进入“十四五规划”的新阶段,地铁隧道工程项目建设进入火热
的发展时期。盾构法作为地铁隧道项目建设的常用方法之一,在施工阶段会受
到作业人员、设备材料、施工管理、周边环境等多种风险因素之间的耦合作用,
使地铁隧道盾构施工安全管理存在一定的风险隐患,而且国内外学者对于地铁
隧道盾构施工的风险耦合研究尚未形成完整的风险管理体系。因此,本文在风
险管理的相关理论基础上,统计归纳 2008-2022 年地铁隧道盾构施工的典型事
故案例,结合相关专家意见整理识别盾构施工的具体风险因素,把盾构施工的
风险耦合系统划分为:人员、物、管理和环境等四个子风险系统,分析地铁隧
道盾构施工风险耦合的机制和作用,以此建立地铁隧道盾构施工风险耦合评价
指标体系,运用 AHP-熵权法计算风险指标的综合权重值,结合云模型的逆向
发生器和功效函数构建风险耦合度模型,对盾构施工风险因素的耦合程度强弱
进行计算。结合系统动力学,以武汉地铁 X 号线盾构施工区间为研究实例,运
用 Vensim PLE 软件建立施工“人-物”风险耦合系统,将耦合度模型中的耦合
系数、各级风险指标的综合权重带入模型中进行动态仿真模拟,通过调整相关
风险耦合系数和仿真时长,观察各风险因素耦合对人-物耦合系统安全风险水平
的变化影响,分析指出异质人-物风险耦合对系统安全风险的影响作用尤为显
著,施工人员的专业技术水平与盾构机选型、组装及调整的风险是关键耦合因
素。
本文通过收集地铁隧道盾构施工的安全事故资料,基于 25 起典型案例分析
和专家建议归纳施工阶段的风险因素,从耦合的角度分析盾构施工风险因素的
作用机制和影响关系,建立风险耦合模型,运用系统动力学研究“人-物”风险
耦合系统的风险水平变化。基于解耦思想提出耦合前、中、后三阶段的风险管
控策略,对完善地铁隧道施工风险管理体系具有一定的理论价值和实际意义。
关键词:盾构施工;风险耦合;耦合度模型;系统动力学;解耦策略


II
Abstract
Currently, China has entered the new stage of the 14th Five-Year Plan, and the
construction of subway tunneling projects has entered a hot development period.
Shield method, as one of the common methods of subway tunnel construction, is
subject to the coupling of various risk factors such as operators, equipment and
materials, construction management and surrounding environment during the
construction stage, which makes the safety management of underpass tunnel shield
construction a certain risk potential, and domestic and foreign scholars have not yet
formed a complete risk management system for the study of risk coupling of underpass
tunnel shield construction. Therefore, in this paper, based on the relevant theories of
risk management, the typical accident cases of subway tunnel shield construction from
2008 to 2022 are statistically summarized, and the specific risk factors of shield
construction are identified by combining relevant expert opinions, and the risk
coupling system of shield construction is divided into four sub-risk systems: personnel,
material, management and environment, etc. The mechanism and role of risk coupling
of subway tunnel shield construction are analyzed, so as to establish The risk coupling
evaluation index system of metro tunnel shield construction is used to calculate the
comprehensive weight value of risk indicators by using AHP-entropy weight method,
and the risk coupling degree model is constructed by combining the inverse generator
and efficacy function of cloud model to calculate the strength of coupling degree of
shield construction risk factors. Combined with the system dynamics, Vensim PLE
software is used to establish the construction "human-material" risk coupling system,
and the coupling coefficients in the coupling degree model and the comprehensive
weights of risk indicators at all levels are brought into the model for dynamic
simulation by adjusting the relevant risk coupling coefficients and simulation duration.
By adjusting the relevant risk coupling coefficients and simulation duration, we
observe the influence of the coupling of various risk factors on the level of safety risk
of the human-material coupling system, and analyze that the heterogeneous
human-material risk coupling has a significant impact on the system safety risk, and
the professional technical level of construction personnel and the risk of shield


III
machine selection, assembly and adjustment are the key coupling factors.
This paper collects the safety accident data of underpass tunnel shield
construction, summarize the risk factors in the construction stage based on 25 typical
cases and expert advice, analyze the mechanism and influence relationship of risk
factors in shield construction from the perspective of coupling, establish a risk
coupling model, and use system dynamics to study the change of risk level in the
"human-material" risk coupling system. Based on the idea of decoupling, the risk
control strategy of the three stages before, during and after coupling is proposed,
which has certain theoretical value and practical significance to improve the risk
management system of underpass tunnel construction.
Keywords: Shield construction; Risk coupling; Coupling degree model; System
dynamics; Decoupling strategy


